From 545d88bc7aaccf33ad59b4722b4be90b9e2788e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laszlo Agocs <laszlo.agocs@qt.io>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:47:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: Store texture upload subresources as a flat sorted list

Each TextureOp in a resource update batch had a dense grid of 6
layers x MAX_MIP_LEVELS (16) containers for the subresource upload
descriptions, i.e. 96 inline QList objects, making a TextureOp 2432
bytes and, with the 32 preallocated ops, an empty
QRhiResourceUpdateBatch 82 KB. The pool grows up to 64 batches and is
never trimmed except via releaseCachedResources(), so with renderers
that acquire and submit many short-lived batches per frame, like Qt
Quick 3D, several MB were spent on empty containers.

Replace the grid with a flat list of (layer, level, description)
entries, stable-sorted by layer and level so the backends see the
same ordering as before, including multiple entries for the same
subresource in submission order. The backends now simply iterate the
list. sizeof(TextureOp) goes from 2432 to 480 bytes, and an empty
batch from 82008 to 19544 bytes on 64-bit.

Change-Id: I76e95221625963cb939eb21cfa24240ab222fd2d
Reviewed-by: Andy Nichols <andy.nichols@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit d17d6fdce8142ad073d884e8f72f00a2e406bb26)
Reviewed-by: Qt Cherry-pick Bot <cherrypick_bot@qt-project.org>
